From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:24:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: thinksmart: report hardware microphone mute

Android consumes SW_MUTE_DEVICE to update audio mute and physical
microphone sensor privacy. SW_MICROPHONE_INSERT describes a connected
microphone instead and does not activate this integration.

GPIO86 is high with the slider in its upper, muted position and low with
the microphones live. Use active-high polarity so switch state one means
muted. The slider already silences both microphone channels in hardware.
Remove the obsolete comment claiming that this switch cannot be modelled.

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View Android integration
Source: https://github.com/msm8953-mainline/linux
Reference: https://github.com/jethac/lenovo-thinksmart-view/blob/fe9c0a58a1a2b7c4893f2ff76ff5c0b90206d458/devices/privacy-switches/ANALYSIS.md
Base-commit: 755ffc44d5d8442adeec8bbaa02108478089c4d7
Apply in filename order within this project.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
@@ -58,16 +58,11 @@
 			linux,input-type = <EV_SW>;
 		};
 
-		/*
-		 * There currently isn't a good way to model a binary microphone mute
-		 * switch. It is a hardware mute switch though, so mics will be muted
-		 * even though it is not reflected in UI.
-		 */
 		mic-mute-swtich {
 			label = "Mic Mute";
-			gpios = <&tlmm 86 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+			gpios = <&tlmm 86 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 			linux,input-type = <EV_SW>;
-			linux,code = <SW_MICROPHONE_INSERT>;
+			linux,code = <SW_MUTE_DEVICE>;
 		};
 
 		volume-up-key {
